{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.canonical","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.lean#L102-L137","doc":"**The trivial model — a `def`, not an `instance`, and not \"faithful\".**\n\nIts docstring said *\"Faithful instance. Carries the explicit research-grade\nconjecture as a sorry.\"* Neither half was true. There is no `sorry`: it sets\n`columnCount _ := 0` and `inTruncation _ := (0 < 2)`, a constantly-true\npredicate that does not mention its argument, so `inTruncation_iff` is\n`(0 < 2) ↔ (0 < 2)` by `decide` and `truncation_holds` is `0 < 2`. Every\nnode is in the truncation because the truncation is everything and every\npartition was declared to have zero columns. A `sorry` would at least be\nvisible to `#print axioms`; this was not.\n\nAs an unconditional `instance` it made `columnCount_nodeOf_lt_k` — the\nbound the MTC truncation pipeline is supposed to consume — an unconditional\ntheorem reading `0 < 2`.\n\nNote it only ever covered `k = 2`; general `k` has no model at all, so the\nrank of the truncated MTC is not exhibited anywhere in this corpus.\n\nDemoted the same way as `ConfinementGradingCorrespondence.canonical`\n(bean `qou-fngs`). Nothing consumed it: the class has no users outside this\nfile.\n\n**Still open:** `conj:root-of-unity-mtc-truncation` — that at\n`q = e^{2πi/k}` the KLR algebra truncates to `MTC_k` with simple objects\nlabelled by partitions of at most `k − 1` columns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.columnCount_nodeOf_lt_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.columnCount_nodeOf_lt_k","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.lean#L87-L100","doc":"Unconditional consequence: every normal form's crystal node has\ncolumn count strictly less than `k`.  Direct consequence of\n`truncation_holds` together with `inTruncation_iff`.  This is\nthe form actually used downstream by the MTC truncation pipeline:\nit bounds the number of columns in the partition labelling each\nGS normal form by the chosen root-of-unity level `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.nodeOf_inTruncation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.nodeOf_inTruncation","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.lean#L76-L85","doc":"Unconditional consequence: every normal form's crystal node is\nin the truncated component (direct from `truncation_holds`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.k_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.k_pos","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.lean#L66-L74","doc":"Unconditional structural lemma: the truncation level `k` is at\nleast `2` (positivity of the MTC rank). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.truncation_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.truncation_holds","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.lean#L61-L61","doc":"**The conjecture itself**: every GS normal form at `q =\ne^{2πi/k}` has `nodeOf T` in the truncated component.  Plays\nthe role of `sorry`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.inTruncation_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.inTruncation_iff","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.lean#L56-L56","doc":"A node is in the truncation iff its column count is `< k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.columnCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.columnCount","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Number of columns of the partition labelling a crystal node. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.inTruncation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.inTruncation","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Predicate: a crystal node is supported on a partition with at\nmost `k - 1` columns.  These are the simple `MTC_k` objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.k_ge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.k_ge_two","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Truncation level `k ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnityMTCTruncation","kind":"class","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RootOfUnityMTCTruncation.lean#L34-L62","doc":"**Root-of-unity MTC truncation (conjecture).**\n\nAt `q = e^{2πi/k}`, the KLR algebra truncates to an MTC `MTC_k`\nwhose simple objects (non-abelian anyons) are labelled by the\ntruncated crystal nodes (partitions with at most `k - 1`\ncolumns). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:root-of-unity-mtc-truncation","label":"conj:root-of-unity-mtc-truncation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/root-of-unity-mtc-truncation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}